## Follow all Lakebase project pages

Context: Lakebase authentication, Settings discovery, and provisioning only
read the first page returned by the Postgres List Projects API. Workspaces
with more projects than the default page size could not resolve projects on
later pages and surfaced a misleading endpoint mismatch.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/LakebaseProjectService.py
   Added a shared raw-API project listing service that follows every pagination token.
2. src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/LakebaseAuth.py
   Used paginated project discovery for endpoint matching and clarified the no-match error.
3. src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py
   Returned Lakebase projects from all pages in Settings.
4. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/provisioner.py
   Resolved newly provisioned projects across all project-list pages.
5. tests/units/core/test_lakebase_project_service.py
   Covered page-token request and aggregation behavior.
6. tests/units/auth/test_lakebase_auth.py
   Added a regression for an endpoint hosted by a page-two project.
7. tests/units/settings/test_lakebase_projects.py
   Covered multi-page Settings project discovery.
8. tests/units/settings/test_lakebase_provision.py
   Added a regression for provisioning project resolution on page two.

